      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The 1836 La Casa de la Centinela Adobe, built by the Spanish colonial era, is a historic landmark in Inglewood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.britannica.com/place/Inglewood",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Inglewood first appeared as a city in the 1910 U.S. Census and became the first California city to declare Martin Luther King Jr. Day.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inglewood%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1946 founding of Fosters Freeze, the first soft‑serve ice‑cream chain in California, began in Inglewood.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
